@ docs/architecture/launch-plan.md:217-237 [Unknown-flag passthrough] terms=4;path=0;heading=4;definition=1;distance=0
217| ## Unknown-flag passthrough
218| 
219| `args.passthrough` holds backend arguments the pre-split did not claim. In the
220| top-level flag region, clud first corrects exact `-deepseek` and exact public
221| option names with a Unicode dash prefix. An unrecognized flag-shaped token
222| is checked against clap's public top-level options: a near miss fails with a
223| suggestion, and any unknown option followed by a key-shaped token fails
224| closed without echoing the key. Other backend flags still pass through
225| byte-for-byte. The `--` separator is the explicit escape hatch and stops
226| correction and validation. A bare-word subcommand near miss is only a note,
227| because the word may be an intentional prompt. The builder appends accepted
228| passthrough after the synthesized prompt and before launch-mode splices.
229| Recognized Claude/Codex-only clud options are rejected for DeepSeek Harness;
230| native `dsh` options can still be passed after `--`.
231| 
232| Operational argv remains unredacted in memory for execution and web-terminal
233| forwarding. Launch records, dry-run JSON, crash reports, and whole-Args debug
234| rendering mask key-shaped values at their output boundaries. This does not
235| remove an inline key from shell history or the operating system process list;
236| vault-backed interactive entry is safer for a live key.
